# 18. Day 2 Troubleshooting Exercise

Give students this intentionally broken YAML:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: nginx-test
spec:
  containers:
    - name: nginx
      image: nginx:notexist
```

Run:

```bash
kubectl apply -f pod.yaml
```

Then:

```bash
kubectl get pods
```

They may see:

```text
ImagePullBackOff
```

Now ask:

> "What should we do?"

First:

```bash
kubectl describe pod nginx-test
```

Look at:

```text
Events:
```

They should find that Kubernetes cannot pull the requested image.

This teaches an important DevOps troubleshooting habit:

```text
Problem
   ↓
kubectl get pods
   ↓
kubectl describe pod
   ↓
Check Events
   ↓
Identify root cause
```

